@startuml
title Sequence Diagram — Observer Pattern\nUser posts a status; Subject notifies Observer automatically

actor User
participant ": FormMain" as Form
participant ": FacebookDataSubject" as Subject
participant ": CachingFacebookProxy" as Proxy
participant ": FacebookService" as FB

note over Form, Subject
  FormMain registered itself as Observer
  in the constructor: r_FacebookService.RegisterObserver(this)
end note

User -> Form : buttonPost_Click()
Form -> Form : tryPostStatus(content)
Form -> Subject : PostStatus(content)

Subject -> Proxy : PostStatus(content)
Proxy -> Proxy : invalidate cached posts
Proxy -> FB : PostStatus(content)
note right of FB : Graph API call\n(takes time)
FB --> Proxy : success
Proxy --> Subject : success

note over Subject
  Write operation succeeded —
  notify all registered observers
end note

Subject -> Subject : notifyObservers(PostPublished)
Subject -> Form : OnFacebookDataChanged(PostPublished)
note right : solid arrow — method call,\nnot a return value

note over Form
  ** Observer Pattern **
  FormMain reacts automatically —
  not called directly by tryPostStatus()
end note

Form -> Form : loadRecentPosts()

Form -> Subject : GetRecentPosts(15)
Subject -> Proxy : GetRecentPosts(15)
Proxy -> FB : user.Posts
note right of FB : Graph API call\n(takes time)
FB --> Proxy : PostCollection
Proxy --> Subject : List<Post>
Subject --> Form : List<Post>
Form -> Form : render updated post cards
Form --> User : recent posts refreshed

@enduml
